// How households spend the coin they hold above a reserve (integration decision I37). Each season a household spends spend_pct_per_season percent of its coin above
// reserve_days days of its members' food (at the base price of grain): wages_pct to idle hands of its village (the poorest first, a day wage each day of service),
// works_pct on building and repair (works_labour_pct of it builders' wages to idle hands, the rest materials bought at the market), goods_pct on craft goods bought at the
// market and used up, alms_pct to the destitute of its village and fief. Historical anchors: the lords' and the Church's spending on retainers, building, cloth, ale and
// alms carried rent and tithe back into the towns; a peasant spent a fifth or so of what he had on cloth, tools and fuel, a burgher more, a lord far more.
